WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.520
Start with a payment request.

00:00:02.520 --> 00:00:04.540
The gateway separates what you ask from

00:00:04.540 --> 00:00:06.900
what an agent is allowed to prepare.

00:00:06.920 --> 00:00:08.640
Amount, recipient, and time

00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.540
are checked before any draft.

00:00:10.560 --> 00:00:13.100
An allowed example passes the policy.

00:00:13.100 --> 00:00:15.100
Increase the amount beyond its limit,

00:00:15.100 --> 00:00:17.120
and the result changes to blocked.

00:00:17.120 --> 00:00:19.980
A failed rule cannot be overridden by
approval.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:22.100
Now change the recipient, or move

00:00:22.100 --> 00:00:24.380
outside the permitted time window.

00:00:24.440 --> 00:00:26.840
Each rejection names the exact rule.

00:00:26.940 --> 00:00:28.500
The local mock executor is not

00:00:28.500 --> 00:00:30.540
called for these denied requests.

00:00:30.560 --> 00:00:33.140
The audit keeps the decisions together.

00:00:33.140 --> 00:00:35.000
In the payment workspace, a shared

00:00:35.000 --> 00:00:38.120
rolling allowance also limits unsigned
exports.

00:00:38.260 --> 00:00:40.860
This demo prepares reviewable information.

00:00:40.860 --> 00:00:42.380
Nothing is signed or sent.
